BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:IU Media School
DTSTART:20261202T230000Z
DTEND:20261203T000000Z
SUMMARY:The Actors Volume Information Session
DESCRIPTION:The Actors Volume is a videogame community and podcast focuse
 d on providing industry insights and exploring the craft behind great gam
 es. Co-founders Jeff Berg (PCAP and voice actor\, 12 years in the industr
 y) and Matthew Brezina (mocap assistant director and producer\, 7 years i
 n the industry) met while shooting Dragon Age: The Veilguard. Matthew and
  Lydia Smyth\, our Director of Social Media Strategy\, are both 2016 grad
 uates of the IU Media School.  On the show\, we sit down with top creativ
 es in the game industry\, including actors\, directors\, casting director
 s and producers\, to talk about the craft behind their work and the paths
  that got them where they are\, so others can follow.  In a session with 
 Game Design students\, we'd love to give students who want to work in gam
 es the chance to ask working professionals how AAA performance capture sh
 oots come together\, hear the many ways people find their way into the in
 dustry\, and get answers about building a career in games.  We'd also lik
 e to introduce our remote internships for Media School students (Producer
 \, Editor and Social Media Writer)\, which offer hands-on experience alon
 gside working industry professionals.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  The Actors Volume is a videogame commun
 ity and podcast focused on providing industry insights and exploring the 
 craft behind great games. Co-founders Jeff Berg (PCAP and voice actor\, 1
 2 years in the industry) and Matthew Brezina (mocap assistant director an
 d producer\, 7 years in the industry) met while shooting Dragon Age: The 
 Veilguard. Matthew and Lydia Smyth\, our Director of Social Media Strateg
 y\, are both 2016 graduates of the IU Media School.</p><p>  On the show\,
  we sit down with top creatives in the game industry\, including actors\,
  directors\, casting directors and producers\, to talk about the craft be
 hind their work and the paths that got them where they are\, so others ca
 n follow.</p><p>  In a session with Game Design students\, we'd love to g
 ive students who want to work in games the chance to ask working professi
 onals how AAA performance capture shoots come together\, hear the many wa
 ys people find their way into the industry\, and get answers about buildi
 ng a career in games.</p><p>  We'd also like to introduce our remote inte
 rnships for Media School students (Producer\, Editor and Social Media Wri
 ter)\, which offer hands-on experience alongside working industry profess
 ionals.</p>
UID:20261202T230000Z-2488604@events.iu.edu
